!CivServer - the Freeciv server
================================

Runs the Freeciv server in a TaskWindow, where you can see its messages
and type server commands (help, list, save, quit, ...).

!Freeciv starts a server by itself when you choose "Start new game". If
that doesn't work on your machine, or you want to see the server:

  1. Double-click !CivServer (the directory with !Freeciv in it must have
     been opened first). A "Freeciv server" window opens.
  2. Double-click !Freeciv and choose "Start new game". It finds the
     running server and plays on it.

Other players on your network can join this server too (port 5556).

The server program and the game data are inside !Freeciv; this
application only starts it. See !Freeciv's !Help for the licences.
